    "promptText": "Listen to the lecture and retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.",
    "audioScript": "Space exploration is a testament to human curiosity and technological advancement. From peering into the stars with early telescopes to landing rovers on Mars, this journey illustrates our relentless pursuit to understand the cosmos. The story of space exploration began with early astronomers like Galileo, who used telescopes to observe celestial bodies. This marked the beginning of a new era in understanding our universe. Fast forward to the 20th century, when the launch of Sputnik, the first artificial satellite, ignited the space race, leading to remarkable milestones including the historic Apollo moon landing in 1969. In recent years, space exploration has entered a new frontier with missions to Mars. Rovers like Curiosity and Perseverance have been exploring the Martian surface, searching for signs of past life and paving the way for future human missions. These rovers represent incredible feats of engineering and symbolize our ongoing quest to explore the unknown. Space exploration is more than just scientific endeavor; it inspires us to look beyond our planet and consider our place in the universe. Each discovery brings new knowledge and raises important questions about our future in space. In conclusion, the journey of space exploration is a continuous voyage of discovery, innovation, and inspiration, demonstrating the boundless potential of human ingenuity.",
