    "promptText": "Listen to the lecture and retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.",
    "audioScript": "I'm going to explore the enduring influence of Greek mythology in modern culture. These ancient myths, more than just old tales, continue to shape our art, literature, and even our understanding of the world. Greek mythology, a rich tapestry of gods, heroes, and monsters, has been a source of inspiration for centuries. Its themes of heroism, adventure, and the human condition resonate deeply, influencing countless works of literature and art. For example, the epic tales of Hercules and Odysseus have been retold in numerous forms, from classical paintings to modern movies. Moreover, Greek mythology extends its influence beyond the arts. It has shaped modern language, with many English words and expressions originating from these ancient stories. Additionally, these myths have provided a framework for understanding human psychology, notably through the work of Freud and Jung, who often used mythological figures to explain complex psychological concepts. In conclusion, the impact of Greek mythology is not confined to the past; it is a living, breathing part of modern culture. Its timeless stories and characters continue to inspire, entertain, and enlighten us, proving that these ancient tales are as relevant today as they were millennia ago.",
