    "promptText": "Listen to the lecture and retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.",
    "audioScript": "Today, let's delve into the enigmatic world of dreams, a fascinating subject that bridges psychology, neuroscience, and even philosophy. Dreams have always been a source of mystery, inspiring countless theories and interpretations. Dreams are not just random images; they are a complex interplay of our subconscious mind. Modern research suggests that dreaming can be a way our brain processes emotions and experiences, integrating them into our memory and learning. For instance, some theories propose that dreams help us solve problems or cope with stress. Additionally, the study of dreams offers insights into various sleep disorders and mental health conditions. By understanding what happens in our brain during different stages of sleep and dreaming, we can better address issues like insomnia, sleepwalking, and nightmares. In conclusion, dreams are more than just nightly escapades of our imagination. They offer a window into our subconscious, providing valuable insights into our mental and emotional well-being.",
