    "audioUrl": null,
    "imageUrl": null,
    "sharedLink": "https://www.apeuni.com/practice/writing?model=swts&num=481&menu=all",
    "promptText": "The recent report on researchers' use of academic libraries was the focus of a workshop to explore its findings and practical use. The workshop aimed at developing and encouraging librarians to understand research practice. The RLUK (Research Libraries UK) reports on the role of research libraries in the production of scholarly research. The report focuses on how research library staff can act as partners and leaders in research, rather than just service providers. The report's findings were discussed in a workshop that brought together researchers and library staff. In the workshop, researchers argued that academic libraries still need to be further improved. Firstly, libraries are shifting from just providing resources to being active collaborators, particularly in digital curation, data management, and open access. Secondly, there is a need to shift library staff’s focus toward proactive research engagement and understanding the \"language\" of researchers.",
