    "audioUrl": null,
    "imageUrl": null,
    "sharedLink": "https://www.apeuni.com/practice/writing?model=essays&num=467&menu=all",
    "promptText": "Professional athletes can earn very high salaries. Many people argue that this is unfair and that other professions deserve higher salaries. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
    "referenceAnswer": "Professional athletes often earn very high salaries, which some consider unfair. However, others argue that their earnings are well-deserved due to their unique skills, entertainment value, and contributions to the economy. This essay will discuss why high salaries for athletes are justified. \nFirstly, professional athletes possess exceptional skills and talents that few can achieve. They dedicate years to rigorous training and sacrifice personal time to excel in their sports. Their achievements inspire millions and serve as a symbol of determination and excellence. Such rare abilities naturally command high rewards, reflecting their value in a competitive market. \nSecondly, athletes bring significant entertainment and economic benefits. Sporting events captivate millions of fans worldwide, creating joy and unity among people. Furthermore, these events generate revenue through ticket sales, merchandise, and media rights, which contribute to economic growth. Athletes are the core reason for this success, and their salaries reflect their pivotal role in the industry. \nIn conclusion, professional athletes earn high salaries because of their exceptional skills, the entertainment they provide, and the economic impact they create. While some may view these earnings as excessive, they are proportional to the value athletes bring to society. Their hard work, dedication, and contributions justify their financial rewards, making their salaries fair in today’s market.",
