    "id": "ape_we_459",
    "apeuniNum": 459,
    "taskType": "WE",
    "section": "writing",
    "title": "#459 Fake News",
    "difficulty": "C1",
    "source": "apeuni_bank",
    "audioUrl": null,
    "imageUrl": null,
    "sharedLink": "https://www.apeuni.com/practice/writing?model=essays&num=459&menu=all",
    "promptText": "Do you agree that social networks should regulate fake news more strictly?",
    "referenceAnswer": "Social networks should regulate fake news more strictly to combat misinformation, protect public trust, and promote civil discourse. In an era where fake news can spread rapidly and influence public opinion, implementing stringent regulations is essential to ensure the accuracy and reliability of information shared on social media platforms. By cracking down on fake news, social networks can uphold their responsibility to provide a trustworthy and conducive online environment for users. \nStrict regulation of fake news is crucial in curbing its spread and promoting the dissemination of accurate information. Misinformation can have detrimental effects on individuals and society, leading to confusion, distrust, and the erosion of factual knowledge. By implementing measures to identify and remove fake news content, social networks can play a pivotal role in combating the proliferation of false information and promoting truthfulness in online discourse. \nRegulating fake news not only maintains the credibility of social networks but also fosters trust among users. When users can rely on social platforms to provide accurate and reliable information, they are more likely to engage in meaningful discussions and interactions. Stricter measures to combat fake news can encourage healthy discourse, prevent polarization fueled by misinformation, and create a more harmonious online community where diverse viewpoints are respected and misinformation is minimized. \nIn conclusion, the strict regulation of fake news on social networks is paramount in safeguarding the integrity of information, fostering trust among users, and promoting constructive conversations.",
