    "promptText": "Do you agree that genetically modified foods are safe for consumption?",
    "referenceAnswer": "Through advancements in genetic engineering, genetically modified (GM) foods offer numerous benefits, including enhanced nutritional value, pest and disease resistance, and increased crop yields. These advancements have the potential to address global food security challenges and contribute to sustainable agriculture practices. \nGenetically modified foods can be tailored to have increased nutritional content, effectively addressing deficiencies in certain vitamins and minerals. By enhancing the nutritional profile of crops through genetic modifications, GM foods have the potential to provide essential nutrients that may be lacking in traditional varieties, thereby improving the overall health and well-being of consumers. \nGM crops can be engineered to resist pests and diseases, reducing the reliance on chemical pesticides and promoting sustainable agricultural practices. By incorporating genetic modifications that confer resistance to common pests and diseases, farmers can reduce the use of harmful chemicals, minimize environmental impact, and ensure a more resilient and productive crop yield. \nIn conclusion, the safety and benefits of genetically modified foods are evident through their enhanced nutritional value, pest and disease resistance, and increased crop yields. As technology continues to advance, genetically modified foods play a crucial role in addressing global food security challenges and promoting sustainable agriculture practices. Embracing the potential of genetically modified foods can lead to a more resilient and efficient food production system, ensuring a safe and sustainable food supply for current and future generations.",
