    "promptText": "What is your opinion on the necessity of bilingual education in a globalized world?",
    "referenceAnswer": "In today's globalized world, the necessity of bilingual education cannot be overstated. Bilingualism is not merely a skill but a tool that enhances communication, opens up global career opportunities, and fosters cultural understanding and empathy. As the world becomes increasingly interconnected, the ability to speak multiple languages is a valuable asset that transcends borders and bridges diverse cultures. \nBilingual education plays a crucial role in facilitating effective communication and collaboration across diverse cultures. Proficiency in multiple languages enables individuals to engage in meaningful dialogues, break down language barriers, and build connections with people from different backgrounds. By mastering more than one language, individuals can navigate cross-cultural interactions with ease, fostering mutual understanding and cooperation in a global context. \nBeing bilingual opens up a wider range of career opportunities in a globalized job market. In an increasingly interconnected world where businesses operate on a global scale, multilingual individuals have a competitive edge. Bilingual professionals can access international job markets, work with diverse teams, and navigate multicultural environments with confidence. The ability to communicate effectively in multiple languages enhances employability and enables individuals to thrive in a globalized workforce. \nIn conclusion, the necessity of bilingual education in a globalized world is evident in its role in enhancing communication, creating global career opportunities, and promoting cultural understanding. Bilingualism is a valuable asset that empowers individuals to connect across borders, seize international prospects, and embrace diversity with empathy and respect. As we navigate an increasingly interconnected world, bilingual education stands as a cornerstone for building bridges between cultures, fostering collaboration, and shaping a more inclusive and harmonious global society.",
