    "id": "ape_we_452",
    "apeuniNum": 452,
    "taskType": "WE",
    "section": "writing",
    "title": "#452 Organic Farming",
    "difficulty": "C1",
    "source": "apeuni_bank",
    "audioUrl": null,
    "imageUrl": null,
    "sharedLink": "https://www.apeuni.com/practice/writing?model=essays&num=452&menu=all",
    "promptText": "To what extent do you think that organic farming can feed the world population?",
    "referenceAnswer": "The question of whether organic farming can sufficiently feed the global population is a complex and pressing issue in today's agricultural landscape. Organic farming practices offer a range of benefits that contribute to sustainable food production and environmental stewardship. \nOrganic farming plays a crucial role in enhancing soil health and fertility, which are essential for sustainable crop production. By avoiding synthetic chemicals and embracing natural methods, organic farmers enrich the soil with nutrients and beneficial microorganisms, fostering long-term productivity and resilience in agricultural systems. \nFurthermore, the practice of crop rotation in organic farming serves as a natural pest control method, reducing the reliance on chemical pesticides. By alternating crops, organic farmers disrupt pest life cycles and prevent the buildup of pest populations, promoting a balanced ecosystem that supports biodiversity and minimizes the risk of crop damage. \nIn conclusion, organic farming holds significant promise in addressing the challenge of feeding the world population sustainably. Through its focus on soil health, pest management, and biodiversity conservation, organic agriculture offers a holistic approach to food production that not only nourishes people but also protects the environment for future generations. Embracing and scaling up organic farming practices can play a pivotal role in ensuring food security while preserving the health of our planet.",
