    "referenceAnswer": "The synthesis of melatonin is in the pineal gland, which is very small. People call this gland \"the seat of the soul\". Melatonin also has a rhythm, which peaks at night. Therefore, it is called the darkness hormone. This means that melatonin occurs at night, and prepares us for the things we do at night.\r\n",
