    "promptText": "Listen to the lecture and write a summary of 50 to 70 words (10 minutes).",
    "audioScript": "At the heart of a thriving honeybee hive, the queen reigns as the vital source of life. Devoted to her duties, the queen tirelessly lays up to 2500 eggs per day, amounting to an incredible two million throughout her lifespan. Comprising the majority of the colony, the hardworking worker bees are all female. Within a typical hive of approximately 30,000 bees, merely 100 of them are males known as drones. With their large eyes and robust bodies, drones rely on the workers for sustenance since they lack the ability to gather pollen or nectar. As the summer wears on, the demanding labor takes its toll on the workers, who live only about 30 days before succumbing to their efforts. However, the hive remains continuously supplied with new generations of bees, eager to begin their toil from the moment they emerge.",
