    "audioScript": "In today's talk, we explore the profound influence of ancient civilizations on our modern society. These early societies, from the Egyptians to the Greeks, have shaped many aspects of our current world, from our political systems to our architectural styles. Take, for instance, the ancient Greeks, whose concepts of democracy and philosophy still underpin much of Western thought. The idea of citizens participating in governance, debated in Athenian forums, laid the groundwork for today's democratic systems. Similarly, Greek philosophy, with thinkers like Plato and Aristotle, continues to influence modern philosophy, ethics, and education. Another example is the Roman Empire, whose legal system forms the basis of many contemporary legal frameworks. Roman law, with its principles of justice and rights, has been adapted and integrated into modern legal systems worldwide. Moreover, ancient architecture and engineering marvels, like the pyramids of Egypt or the Roman aqueducts, not only demonstrate early ingenuity but also continue to inspire modern engineering and architecture.",
