    "promptText": "Why does the woman mention her boss?",
    "audioScript": "Giving feedback is hard. It can be uncomfortable. And on some level, you worry that you could hurt the other person's feelings because that's sometimes what happens when you give feedback. But I want to say that getting good feedback can feel like an act of generosity, and I've experienced it firsthand. I had a boss who put so much thought and care into the way that she talked to me about my work, I felt like she was really invested, and I always felt better after talking to her and getting feedback. So really, constructive, actionable feedback is a gift. And in this episode, we're going to teach you how to give it. But don't worry; we have another episode coming about how to receive feedback, too, because, you know, we're completists like that. What can I say? And while we're mostly focusing on giving feedback in a workplace setting, by all means, please take this wisdom from Massella into your whole life. You won't regret it.",
