    "audioScript": "What are the essential elements that make a conversation truly a great conversation? And humility would be one basic design principle that we should all start from. The kind of humility I’m talking about is the kind that you can’t set aside. Because the world is an incredibly complicated place. None of us can ever have the full lock on truth. We can only see the world from a particular vantage point. And that means that our knowledge is going to be going to have special insight because of our vantage point but it’s also going to be limited because of our vantage point. And so that sort of like limited knowledge that we can have about the world means that we must enter into any conversation with a deep sense of...",
