    "sharedLink": "https://www.apeuni.com/practice/listening?model=hiws&num=358&menu=all",
    "audioScript": "There is something hard to resist about cherries. The small red fruit is a popular seasonal food around the world. In northern areas, cherry trees are just beginning to produce flowers. The cherry is a member of the same family of plants as the rose. It is closely related to the plum. Like cherry trees, plum trees also flower in early spring. Cherries are thought to be native to Western Asia. There are two major kinds of cherries harvested in the world: sweet and sour. Sour cherries are not eaten fresh because they contain little sugar. Instead, they are processed to start prepared foods like jellies and pies and to start alcoholic drinks. The United States is a major producer of sour cherries. Among the states, Michigan is the top producer.",
