    "audioScript": "They may be our cousins, but orangutans and other primates are nowhere near humans in terms of technological achievement, social organization or culture. As humans, capacity for building off one another, an integral part of our so called cumulative culture that has allowed us to build up so much in so little time. But how do we develop such advanced methods of learning in the first place? Kevin Leyland of the University of St Andrews spoke with me about his team's quest to pinpoint the social and cognitive process that underlie humans ability to acquire and transmit knowledge.",
