    "audioScript": "Well there… there… there’s a positive obligation on the bank to ensure that the people who are signing a loan guarantee, know what they’re doing. Loan guarantees are ... er ... kind of unique in that … in that someone is giving security or a guarantee and placing themselves at risk for someone else, and they receive nothing material in return. So you’ve got to ask yourself why is this person doing this, do they know what they’re doing? They’re risking a lot, and not really getting anything back for it. So the imperative is that the bank must ensure that these people know what they’re doing, and that they fully understand the implications of what they’re doing, and they know that their properties may be sold if another person doesn’t meet their obligations.",
